{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/extras/1484a9614c4958e4d921a074ba287dd7.avif?t=1770834311\" width=616 height=128 /></span><u><strong>Case 42: The Redwood Files</strong></u> is a <strong>Narrative Horror Adventure</strong> game where you play as a Detective and unravel the mystery of a seemingly simple murder case that unfolds itself into something much bigger and scarier.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It is inspired by the melancholic moods of Twin Peaks &amp; the atmospheric feel of Silent hill.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/extras/e54d7bcf8d63b91e4a59f40d00a74a14.avif?t=1770834311\" width=616 height=64 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/extras/506749f586d13d90c91ea94a26e36b0a.avif?t=1770834311\" width=616 height=128 /></span><strong> </strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u><strong><i>\u201cA demo is in the works and will be available in the near future. Wishlist the game to be notified when it's live!\u201d</i></strong></u></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/extras/e54d7bcf8d63b91e4a59f40d00a74a14.avif?t=1770834311\" width=616 height=64 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><u>The Redwood Files</u></strong> is a game that takes place in a quite secluded small town on the Hills of North East India, that is partly welcoming to the detective, partly unwelcoming. This game involves the player making deductions about crime scenes, the loop is to investigate places, talk to folks, get leads, solve puzzles in both worlds, progress, get further leads, connect dots, manage time. You traverse through two realms, one being the normal world where Detective does scene and item investigation, talk to folks and get leads on cases while in other world the Detective faces the real horror of the game, where, while encountering inhumane hostile entities, you further learn about something relevant to the case.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3586150?t=1770834311","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3586150?t=1770834311","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/f7746248c4c7f53c673f5302fb6bad867f8fe1b6/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1770834311","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/f7746248c4c7f53c673f5302fb6bad867f8fe1b6/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1770834311","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Partial Controller Support","id":18},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/extras/1484a9614c4958e4d921a074ba287dd7.avif?t=1770834311\" width=616 height=128 /></span><u><strong>Case 42: The Redwood Files</strong></u> is a <strong>Narrative Horror Adventure</strong> game where you play as a Detective and unravel the mystery of a seemingly simple murder case that unfolds itself into something much bigger and scarier.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It is inspired by the melancholic moods of Twin Peaks &amp; the atmospheric feel of Silent hill.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/extras/e54d7bcf8d63b91e4a59f40d00a74a14.avif?t=1770834311\" width=616 height=64 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/extras/506749f586d13d90c91ea94a26e36b0a.avif?t=1770834311\" width=616 height=128 /></span><strong> </strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u><strong><i>\u201cA demo is in the works and will be available in the near future. Wishlist the game to be notified when it's live!\u201d</i></strong></u></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/extras/e54d7bcf8d63b91e4a59f40d00a74a14.avif?t=1770834311\" width=616 height=64 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><u>The Redwood Files</u></strong> is a game that takes place in a quite secluded small town on the Hills of North East India, that is partly welcoming to the detective, partly unwelcoming. This game involves the player making deductions about crime scenes, the loop is to investigate places, talk to folks, get leads, solve puzzles in both worlds, progress, get further leads, connect dots, manage time. You traverse through two realms, one being the normal world where Detective does scene and item investigation, talk to folks and get leads on cases while in other world the Detective faces the real horror of the game, where, while encountering inhumane hostile entities, you further learn about something relevant to the case.</p>","developers":["A DeadGame Studio"],"genres":[{"description":"Adventure","id":"25"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3586150/b6821f1278d2dfae3b68d45c9cb86da1a27ddc0f/header.jpg?t=1770834311","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[],"movies":[{"dash_av1":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/3586150/875185/0479c3b775afddd2e2495499d96447311e152afc/1750462090/dash_av1.mpd